{
  "name": "What to Expect During a Roof Damage Evaluation",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1: So, you've got some concerns about your roof after a recent storm o…",
      "text": "So, you've got some concerns about your roof after a recent storm or maybe it's just getting older. A proper roof damage evaluation isn't just a quick glance; it's a thorough process designed to give you a complete picture. First, an experienced evaluator will look into your roof's history, like its age and any past repairs, to understand its baseline. Then, they'll meticulously examine both the exterior and interior, including the attic, using photos or videos to document every bit of damage. This helps differentiate storm-related issues from normal aging. Our goal is to provide clear findings and honest repair recommendations, ensuring you know exactly what's needed without any surprises.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2: What to Prepare Before You Start Before your evaluation, it really…",
      "text": "What to Prepare Before You Start Before your evaluation, it really helps to have a few things ready. Gather any old repair records or photos you have of your roof, especially if they're dated. Dig out your insurance policy documents too, if you're considering a claim. It's also super important to avoid getting on the roof yourself after a storm; it can be dangerous, especially if it's wet or already compromised. Leave the ladder work to the pros. Being prepared helps your evaluator focus on the important stuff and gets you closer to a solution faster.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3: Need a professional opinion on your roof's condition?",
      "text": "Need a professional opinion on your roof's condition? Reach out to Discounted Roofing Co. today.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    }
  ],
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
